
                           IMBEDDED COLOUR CODES

  There are two methods of changing colours in Telegard 3.0, for use in 
  display files (*.MSG), in the language strings, menu prompts and in 
  message text (where not stripped).

  The two methods allow the use of the full range of colours -- all 
  foreground and background combinations in low and high intensity, and of 
  course the blinking versions of those as well.  This provides a total of 
  256 different colour combinations.

  The first method is the most compact, and was added since it will keep 
  SysOp definable strings/menus to a shorter length (for more text). The 
  second method is easier to use, and was implemented so that users don't 
  need to remember the compact codes.

  Both methods use a sequence of three characters to change the colour - 
  the first method changes both the foreground and background at the same 
  time.  The second method changes one at a time (so to change both the 
  foreground and background, two sequences are required).

  I highly suggest using the *first* method.  It's faster (and more 
  efficient to part) and also more compact, and likely to be the method 
  that is retained if one has to go. ;)

  I. Some preliminary notes:
  
  For those looking for "Yellow" -- "Yellow" is the high intensity BROWN.
  Why? I don't know (ask them DOS programmers from way back).  Likewise,
  magenta and pink are also linked together (although this is far more 
  intuitive).
  
  II. The first method:

  The colour sequence indicator (`), followed by two characters from 0 to
  9, A to F to form the colour code.  The colour codes are listed below for
  your convenience (low and high intensity side by side).

  REGULAR
           Black   Blue    Green   Cyan    Red     Magenta Brown   White
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Black   | 00 08 | 01 09 | 02 0A | 03 0B | 04 0C | 05 0D | 06 0E | 07 0F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Blue    | 10 18 | 11 19 | 12 1A | 13 1B | 14 1C | 15 1D | 16 1E | 17 1F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Green   | 20 28 | 21 29 | 22 2A | 23 2B | 24 2C | 25 2D | 26 2E | 27 2F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Cyan    | 30 38 | 31 39 | 32 3A | 33 3B | 34 3C | 35 3D | 36 3E | 37 3F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Red     | 40 48 | 41 49 | 42 4A | 43 4B | 44 4C | 45 4D | 46 4E | 47 4F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Magenta | 50 58 | 51 59 | 52 5A | 53 5B | 54 5C | 55 5D | 56 5E | 57 5F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Brown   | 60 68 | 61 69 | 62 6A | 63 6B | 64 6C | 65 6D | 66 6E | 67 6F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  White   | 70 78 | 71 79 | 72 7A | 73 7B | 74 7C | 75 7D | 76 7E | 77 7F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+

  BLINKING COLOURS
                                                           
           Black   Blue    Green   Cyan    Red     Magenta Brown   White
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Black   ³ 80 88 | 81 89 | 82 8A | 83 8B | 84 8C | 85 8D | 86 8E | 87 8F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Blue    ³ 90 98 | 91 99 | 92 9A | 93 9B | 94 9C | 95 9D | 96 9E | 97 9F |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Green   ³ A0 A8 | A1 A9 | A2 AA | A3 AB | A4 AC | A5 AD | A6 AE | A7 AF |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Cyan    ³ B0 B8 | B1 B9 | B2 BA | B3 BB | B4 BC | B5 BD | B6 BE | B7 BF |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Red     ³ C0 C8 | C1 C9 | C2 CA | C3 CB | C4 CC | C5 CD | C6 CE | C7 CF |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Magenta ³ D0 D8 | D1 D9 | D2 DA | D3 DB | D4 DC | D5 DD | D6 DE | D7 DF |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  Brown   ³ E0 E8 | E1 E9 | E2 EA | E3 EB | E4 EC | E5 ED | E6 EE | E7 EF |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
  White   ³ F0 F8 | F1 F9 | F2 FA | F3 FB | F4 FC | F5 FD | F6 FE | F7 FF |
          +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+

  III. The second method:

  The colour sequence indicator (|), followed by two characters (0..9)
  which form the colour code.  This method changes only the foreground
  or the background at any given time.  To change both attributes, two
  colour sequences need to be used.

            Fore                Back              Blink
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  Black   | 00 08 |    Black   | 16 |    Black   |  24 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  Blue    | 01 09 |    Blue    | 17 |    Blue    |  25 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  Green   | 02 10 |    Green   | 18 |    Green   |  26 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  Cyan    | 03 11 |    Cyan    | 19 |    Cyan    |  27 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  Red     | 04 12 |    Red     | 20 |    Red     |  28 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  Magenta | 05 13 |    Magenta | 21 |    Magenta |  29 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  Brown   | 06 14 |    Brown   | 22 |    Brown   |  30 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+
  White   | 07 15 |    White   | 23 |    White   |  31 |
          +-------+            +----+            +-----+

  The "|" characters in the boxes to not translate into colour codes 
  because they are not immediately followed by a number (but rather by
  other characters (i.e. "-" or " ").  This is important to note if you 
  need to hse the "|" character anywhere.

